Brock Lesnar is a professional wrestler, mixed martial artist, and former amateur wrestler and professional American football player. He is currently signed to WWE on the Raw brand and has won numerous championships, including the WWE Championship, World Heavyweight Championship, and IWGP Heavyweight Championship. Lesnar has also had a successful career in mixed martial arts, winning the UFC Heavyweight Championship and being a top contender in the division.

Lesnar was born on July 12, 1977, in Webster, South Dakota, and grew up on a dairy farm. He attended Bismarck State College and the University of Minnesota, where he won the NCAA Division I heavyweight wrestling championship in 2000. Lesnar then signed with the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) in 2000 and was sent to its developmental territory, Ohio Valley Wrestling, where he formed a tag team with Shelton Benjamin.

Lesnar debuted on WWF television in 2002 and quickly became a top contender, winning the King of the Ring tournament and the WWE Undisputed Championship. He also became the youngest WWE Champion at age 25, a record previously held by The Rock. Lesnar has had a successful career in professional wrestling, winning numerous championships and headlining numerous pay-per-view events.

In addition to his wrestling career, Lesnar has also had a successful career in mixed martial arts, winning the UFC Heavyweight Championship and being a top contender in the division. Lesnar has also been involved in various other ventures, including a stint in the National Football League (NFL) and a career in professional American football.

Lesnar has been managed by Paul Heyman throughout his professional wrestling career and has been known for his intense and physical style in the ring. He has headlined numerous pay-per-view events for both the WWE and UFC, including WrestleMania XIX, WrestleMania 31, UFC 100, and UFC 116. In 2015, an ESPN.com article referred to Lesnar as "the most accomplished athlete in pro wrestling history." 

Overall, Brock Lesnar is a highly accomplished athlete with a successful career in both professional wrestling and mixed martial arts. He has won numerous championships and has been a top contender in both divisions, and his intense and physical style in the ring has made him a fan favorite. 

